1. Docker Image **
A DOCKER image is a blueprint that contains:
-Your application code
-Runtime (Java, Node, Python, etc.)
-Libraries
-Dependencies
-Configuration
2. Docker Container **
A CONTAINER is a running instance of that image.
It is an isolated environment where your application actually runs.

Docker = Build & run one container **
Kubernetes = Manage thousands of containers automatically **
Think of Kubernetes as:
-A traffic controller
-A doctor (self‑healing)
-A load balancer
-A deployment manager
-A resource optimizer
-All working together.

kubectl get pods
kubectl describe pod <name>
kubectl logs <name> -f
kubectl exec -it <name> -- sh
