  *****Creatinng Dockerfile and running the container locally*****
1. add Dockerfile to the project root with the following content:
create Dockerfile with the following content:
      FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jre-jammy
	  WORKDIR /app
      COPY /target/book-finder-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar app.jar
      ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"]


2. build the docker image with the following command:
	  docker build -t myapp:latest .
	  
3. to see docket images run the following command:
       docker images	  

4. run locally with the following command:
       docker run -p 8096:8096 myapp:latest
  
5. run your Docker container with the following command: (same step as step 3)
       docker run -p 8080:8080 myapp:latest
  
6. check if the container is running with the following command:
      docker ps
 
7.stop the container with the following command:
      docker stop <container_id>
 
